---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/drip-vs-sendlane';
const title = 'Drip vs Sendlane for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "For a Shopify team considering Drip and Sendlane, support scope and email frequency deserve separate examination. Sendlane advertises send-based pricing and tiered support. A large contact list does not by itself establish its cost, and a support promise does not transfer responsibility for your customer data.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Sendlane priced by contacts?",
    "answer": "Sendlane currently describes send-based pricing with unlimited contacts. Obtain a quote using the intended send calendar and support package."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does every Sendlane plan include identical migration support?",
    "answer": "No assumption of identical scope is justified. Its pricing page lists support tiers and annual-contract conditions for dedicated services."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should an audio retailer rehearse?",
    "answer": "Use warranty registration, an unresolved support case, refund and replacement shipment to check journey eligibility and handover responsibilities."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Drip require an unsupported self-serve migration?",
    "answer": "Do not assume that. Check available assistance and scope for the actual offer, then assign ownership for any work that remains internal."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Drip vs Sendlane for Shopify</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">For a Shopify team considering Drip and Sendlane, support scope and email frequency deserve separate examination. Sendlane advertises send-based pricing and tiered support. A large contact list does not by itself establish its cost, and a support promise does not transfer responsibility for your customer data.</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Price send volume and specify migration ownership</h2>
    <p>This comparison is an editorial evaluation framework, checked against primary product information on 24 November 2026. The exercises below are proposed tests; no merchant trial or performance result is claimed.</p>
    <h2>Compare operating plans, not team stereotypes</h2>
    <p>Drip provides email workflow tools and a Shopify connection. Sendlane lists ecommerce integration, behavior-based automation and support packages. It is misleading to assume Drip users must work without help or that all Sendlane customers receive the same managed service. Request a written support scope for each offer. The decision is whether the specific package closes your implementation gap at a sustainable ongoing cost.</p>
    <h2>Proposed migration job: warranty before cross-sell</h2>
    <p>Consider a hypothetical audio retailer moving a long-consideration post-purchase program. The first message explains setup, a later step requests warranty registration, and cross-sell should exclude customers with unresolved support cases. Identify where registration and case status originate. Verify that the required fields or events reach each candidate; Shopify order data alone does not establish a warranty or support integration.</p>
    <h2>Turn the handoff into an acceptance artifact</h2>
    <p>Give both vendors the same sample records: registered owner, unregistered owner, open support case, refunded order and replacement shipment. Write the intended journey for each. Have the proposed implementation owner build the sequence and supply a map of triggers, waits, exits and missing-data behavior. Ask your future operator to change the registration reminder and remove a cross-sell step. Record actual effort during the exercise rather than asserting a platform builds it in an afternoon.</p>
    <h2>Do not outsource the purchase exit assumption</h2>
    <p>Place an internal order and refund it while the proposed flow waits. Inspect whether the profile exits, remains eligible or needs a separate rule. Check a replacement shipment that should not restart the marketing sequence. If a field arrives late, decide whether to wait, skip the promotion or route to manual review. This exposes migration semantics that a copied email template will not reveal.</p>
    <h2>Support scope needs named deliverables</h2>
    <p>Sendlane lists Professional, Enterprise and Enterprise Plus support differences and states that dedicated support services require an annual contract. Confirm exactly which migration, integration configuration, review cadence and deliverability tasks your offer includes. Ask who writes copy, maps custom events and signs off on suppression imports. A named owner and handover document are more useful than assuming white-glove means every workflow is rebuilt for every plan.</p>
    <h2>Send-based and person-based budgets diverge</h2>
    <p>Sendlane describes unlimited contacts with billing based on sends. Drip pricing considers active people and email volume. Build two calendars using your own numbers: a quiet period with warranty education and a promotion-heavy period. Count automation sends as well as broadcasts and ask how seasonal peaks and overages are handled. Do not use the Sendlane page calculator placeholder as a verified quote or label one product a universal support premium.</p>
    <h2>Migration labor is distinct from subscription cost</h2>
    <p>Price field mapping, template work, authentication, data transfer, acceptance testing and operator training separately. If a package includes some tasks, subtract only work it actually covers. For a hypothetical labor estimate, six hours at $50 per hour equals $300; that is illustrative internal labor, not a supplier fee or promised saving. Add ongoing maintenance rather than assuming the first migration is the entire operating cost.</p>
    <h2>Launch without discarding the old logic</h2>
    <p>Inventory the live Drip or other-provider sequences and suppression records before the move. Activate the accepted warranty path only after recording which old steps have been paused. Retain the old maps and event definitions for rollback. Run the operator handover before enabling broad cross-sell. Choose Drip when its demonstrated workflow and support arrangement fit the team; choose Sendlane when its demonstrated implementation and volume economics fit better. Hold the decision if custom events or contract scope remain unresolved.</p>
    <h2>Primary sources and limits</h2><ul>
      <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sendlane.com/pricing">Sendlane billing and support tiers</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/4424695491725-Connect-Your-Shopify-Store">Drip Shopify connection</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="https://www.drip.com/pricing">Drip current pricing</a></li>
    </ul><p>Product documentation establishes advertised scope. Account access, integration latency and commercial terms still require confirmation for the proposed setup. No runtime tests were performed for this comparison.</p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-drip">Klaviyo vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/alternatives/klaviyo-alternative">Best Klaviyo alternatives</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/high-aov">Email apps for high-AOV stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/guides/migration">ESP migration guide</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Drip vs Sendlane FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
